def about(data,locations):
 f=next(x for x in data if x['slug']=='pratapgad')
 return f'''<section class="about-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">OUR PURPOSE / OUR PEOPLE</p><h1>Keep the<br><em>stories alive.</em></h1><p>Swarajya Explorer brings Maharashtra’s forts, landscapes and layered histories into one place — an invitation to look closer, learn more and explore with care.</p><a class="outline-button" href="#connect">Contact & connect ↗</a></div><figure>{img(f,large=True)}<figcaption>PRATAPGAD · MAHARASHTRA</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="wrap about-values"><article><span>01 / DISCOVER</span><h2>Beyond the walls.</h2><p>Find places through authentic photography, geographical context and the structures that still survive.</p></article><article><span>02 / UNDERSTAND</span><h2>History with context.</h2><p>Explore the legacy of Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj, Chhatrapati Sambhaji Maharaj and the many people and communities connected with these forts.</p></article><article><span>03 / CARE</span><h2>A shared inheritance.</h2><p>Thoughtful visits and careful research help people appreciate heritage without damaging the places or simplifying their histories.</p></article></section>
<section class="wrap creator-profile"><div class="creator-monogram" aria-hidden="true">PVC</div><div><p class="eyebrow">MEET THE CREATOR</p><h2>Pranav Vinod Chame</h2><p>Creator and developer of Swarajya Explorer. This independent project combines website development with an interest in exploring Maharashtra’s forts and presenting Maratha history accessibly.</p><p>Inspired by <strong>Tanshiq and Karan.</strong></p><a class="text-button" href="#connect">Get in touch ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="connect" class="wrap connect-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">CONTACT & CONNECT</p><h2>A good story<br><em>starts a conversation.</em></h2><p>Share feedback, suggest a correction or discuss a collaboration. For historical or location corrections, include the fort name and a reliable source.</p></div><div class="connect-links"><a href="mailto:pranavchame1@gmail.com"><span>Email Pranav<br><small>pranavchame1@gmail.com</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://www.instagram.com/pranavdecoded/"><span>Follow the journey<br><small>@pranavdecoded</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="wrap about-method"><h2 id="method">Our research approach.</h2><p>The published catalogue contains {len(data)} photographed forts and {locations} source-referenced map locations. Each profile links its research and photo credits. Entries without a verified photograph are kept outside the public catalogue. Exact dates, elevations and routes remain unknown where the evidence is insufficient.</p><p>Historical associations do not establish a fort’s builder or an uninterrupted period of possession. Trek grades are provisional source interpretations; photographs and coordinates have not been independently authenticated by a field survey. Read the references and check current access locally.</p><h2 id="responsible">Explore with respect.</h2><ul><li>Check weather, permissions and access before travelling.</li><li>Use established paths and qualified local guidance for exposed or unfamiliar terrain.</li><li>Carry drinking water, leave enough daylight and confirm return transport.</li><li>Respect sacred spaces, local communities and fragile masonry.</li><li>Carry waste back. Never carve names or remove historical material.</li></ul><p>This is an independent educational project with no official affiliation to heritage authorities.</p><a class="outline-button" href="sources.html">Sources & photograph credits ↗</a></section>'''
